{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "07W7", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-change-of-field}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cd38e76d7aa5abcb335b686347a3725eaaf0d5c99440bdbc43d0f5be8c62cf8b", "source_text": "Change of residue field", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a6106ee45a4fc5bd4c0d18ce657a1cc2155c88ccbf3b828e6dae284432123efc", "unit_id": "tag:07W7:title"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$k$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Lambda \\to k$", "MATH_0004": "$k$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0007": "$k$", "MATH_0008": "$k$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}_{\\Lambda, k}$", "MATH_0010": "$k$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-CLambda}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:47d6f17e80909006b62bc681457617102f85b08107d29b3223b96710562a798d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6e83718c871bc1821353b7b8879cda149324b02c75d1c87572674c91bf6d6f38", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we quickly discuss what happens if we replace the residue\nfield <MATH_0001> by a finite extension. Let <MATH_0002> be a Noetherian ring and\nlet <MATH_0003> be a finite ring map where <MATH_0004> is a field. Throughout\nthis whole chapter we have used <MATH_0005> to denote the\ncategory of Artinian local <MATH_0006>-algebras whose residue field is\nidentified with <MATH_0007>, see Definition <REF_0001>.\nHowever, since in this section we will discuss what happen when we change\n<MATH_0008> we will instead use the notation <MATH_0009> to\nindicate the dependence on <MATH_0010>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7c0174cc9bdad91945e0d66d2d7afa2a33e83ccd69fe1e14f1a75fad3feccc19", "unit_id": "tag:07W7:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "situation", "parent_tag": "07W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Lambda \\to k \\to l$", "MATH_0003": "$k$", "MATH_0004": "$l$", "MATH_0005": "$l/k$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}_{\\Lambda, l}$", "MATH_0007": "$B$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}_{\\Lambda, k}$", "MATH_0009": "$A$", "MATH_0010": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-comparison}\n\\mathcal{C}_{\\Lambda, l} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{C}_{\\Lambda, k},\n\\quad\nB \\longmapsto B \\times_l k\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0011": "$p : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{C}_{\\Lambda, k}$", "MATH_0012": "$$\np_{l/k} : \\mathcal{F}_{l/k} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{C}_{\\Lambda, l}\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}_{l/k}(B) = \\mathcal{F}(B \\times_l k)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{situation}\n\\label{situation-change-of-fields}\n", "suffix": "\\end{situation}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:892a8ae8ecd54773a9c23c03a3f884a97e820dd05b8ffd67eeb509aa418cdf38", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a8d4902cc6edc5c227b4139b4724e4150b6677261271635f90569ac57d8e4038", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a Noetherian ring and let <MATH_0002> be a finite\nring maps where <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are fields. Thus <MATH_0005> is a finite\nextensions of fields. A typical object of <MATH_0006> will be\ndenoted <MATH_0007> and a typical object of <MATH_0008> will be\ndenoted <MATH_0009>. We define\n<MATH_0010>\nGiven a category cofibred in groupoids\n<MATH_0011> we obtain\nan associated category cofibred in groupoids\n<MATH_0012>\nby setting <MATH_0013>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:06b8491e602eebe3e54efdbada41bfe02ac4eb97c21a3d70b276553e06e6d460", "unit_id": "tag:07W8:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B \\times_l k \\subset B$", "MATH_0002": "\\begin{align*}\n[k : k']\\ \\text{length}_{B \\times_l k}(B \\times_l k) & =\n\\text{length}_\\Lambda(B \\times_l k) \\\\\n& \\leq \\text{length}_\\Lambda(B) \\\\\n& = [l : k']\\ \\text{length}_B(B) < \\infty\n\\end{align*}", "MATH_0003": "$B \\times_l k$", "MATH_0004": "$B \\times_l k$", "MATH_0005": "$k$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n(B_1 \\times_B B_2) \\times_l k =\n(B_1 \\times_l k) \\times_{(B \\times_l k)} (B_2 \\times_l k)\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}_{l/k}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-comparison}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-length}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-artinian-finite-length}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{equation-comparison}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{remark-localize-cofibered-groupoid}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0cf2a68134a47e9c8377ce67ca041f9941331cb75eea40c04dd13158500c22d6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3c2dc265d720b88adb70a41a67860229e2f22870b2c51476247ab07fd9030132", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe functor (<REF_0001>) makes sense:\nbecause <MATH_0001> we have\n<MATH_0002>\n(see Lemma <REF_0002>) hence <MATH_0003> is Artinian\n(see Algebra, Lemma <REF_0003>).\nThus <MATH_0004> is an Artinian local ring with\nresidue field <MATH_0005>. Note that (<REF_0004>)\ncommutes with fibre products\n<MATH_0006>\nand transforms surjective ring maps into surjective ring maps.\nWe use the ``expensive'' notation <MATH_0007> to prevent confusion\nwith the construction of Remark <REF_0005>.\nHere are some elementary observations.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5fe318b702e9127fda6714ec955f17fb0f9f62905aca4db2bc146a52dc598488", "unit_id": "tag:07W7:prose-0002"}
